      "problem": "$\\int ({csch}^{2}⁡x-4{sech}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)={sech}^{2}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\int {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)=-{csch}^{2}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({csch}^{2}⁡x-4{sech}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-4\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
